AB  - Discusses an interdisciplinary age-specific approach to psychiatric care for geriatric patients at a medical center. It is noted that these patients are admitted to the center most frequently for depression. The admission procedure is based on the desire to maintain a milieu without excessive medical illness or disruptive behavior. Treatment modalities include milieu, group, individual, and family therapies; a supportive environment that minimizes stress is emphasized. Prevention of falls in psychogeriatric patients, who appear to be more vulnerable than regular geriatric patients, is discussed. The formation of a geriatric psychiatric unit in a general hospital is endorsed for effective treatment. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
