AB  - Evaluated whether a 3-phase multicomponent treatment package could be successfully implemented with individuals who engage in self-injurious hand mouthing maintained by sensory consequences in the context of both individual and small group settings. Three ambulatory Ss (aged 21–40 yrs) with profound mental retardation participated on an individual basis followed by treatment within a group setting. Generalization of the intervention results to the natural living environment was then analyzed. Using an ABAB experimental design, the effectiveness of brief response interruption followed by the introduction of a preferred leisure item to reduce hand mouthing during 15-min intervention sessions was analyzed. Results show that the intervention could be successfully implemented during individual and small group sessions and during group sessions conducted in the natural environment. These replicate those obtained by D. Irwin et al (1996). (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
