AB  - Describes an effective summer day program for the mentally impaired elderly. The helping principles applied in a life model and interactionally oriented group and milieu approach are discussed and illustrated. The program attempts to restore participants' sense of self, provide opportunities for recall through doing, talking, and sharing common feelings. The provision of a positive 'here and now' experience that recognizes and bolsters strengths makes it more attractive to live more fully here and now. Even the most regressed patients improved in outlook and functioning as a result of the group experience. (12 ref) (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
