AB  - Physicians have been slow to acknowledge the presence and significance of alcohol and other drug dependencies in the older adult population. Because of the deleterious effects of substance abuse throughout the life span, to neglect this phenomenon in the elderly is to lose an opportunity to enhance the biopsychosocial well-being of a significant number of older patients.
