AB  - The article offers an overview of the "Principles of Drug Addiction Treatment: A Research-Based Guide," from the U.S. National Institute on Drug Abuse (NIDA). The guiding principles for home health nurses include the need to know the fact that there is no single treatment appropriate for all individuals, the need for treatment to be readily available, that effective treatment attends to multiple needs of an individual and that a patient may develop a need for medical services, family therapy, vocational rehabilitation, social and legal services. Also included are the importance of remaining in treatment for an adequate period, the significance of individual and/or group counseling and other behavioral therapies, and the need to treat both addiction and mental disorder in an integrated way.
