AB  - Alcoholism treatment often encourages involvement in Alcoholics Anonymous (AA). Little provision is made for women with social phobia (SP), who have been reported to have worse outcomes in 12-step facilitation (TSF) relative to cognitive behavioral therapy. This study examined whether SP moderated the effects of gender for these women in TSF. One hundred thirty-three SP alcoholics assigned to TSF (35 females and 98 males) in Project MATCH were compared to a no-SP control group. SP women drank earlier and more intensely than no-SP women and all males, had equivalent completion of Step 5, and were less likely to acquire a sponsor during TSF. Copyright © Taylor & Francis Group, LLC.
