AB  - Describes a retrospective longitudinal treatment utilization study of 56 chronic schizophrenics (aged 18–44 yrs) who began their treatment careers during the deinstitutionalization era. All psychiatric services provided to each S since 1st treatment were assessed. The group was primarily male and was characterized by histories of drug abuse and violence. Treatment utilization was heavy, discontinuous, and episodic, with such patterns intensifying for Ss with histories of drug abuse. Most Ss became long-stay hospital residents. Clinical and mental health policy implications are discussed. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
