AB  - Using data from a general population telephone survey of 24,778 current drinkers from four CA & two SC communities, Tobit models are estimated to determine the influence of background demographic characteristics on the selection of drinking locations net of other model control variables. Distinct patterns of premise utilization are found to be associated with age, gender, & ethnic subgroups. Additionally, these patterns are differentially linked to drinking & driving, suggesting that patterns of outlet utilization are differentially linked to acute drinking problems (eg, drunken driving & alcohol-related car crashes). Observed differences in outlet utilization patterns between age, gender, & ethnic subgroups imply that preventive interventions should take into account the manner in which these subpopulations make use of drinking venues. 4 Tables, 17 References. Adapted from the source document.
