AB  - The aim of this report was to determine whether the Tokyo Metropolitan Institute of Gerontology (TMIG) index of competence and the Zung Self-rating Depression Scale (SDS) scores of older persons could be improved as a result of the FIT home visit program. This study was conducted in the rural towns of Shinhidaka and Hidaka in Hokkaido, Japan. A total of 252 participants aged 65 years or older living at home and receiving preventive services or a community long-term care prevention project according to the Japanese social long-term care insurance system were enrolled and randomly assigned to an intervention group. In conclusion, no significant improvement was found in the Tokyo Metropolitan Institute of Gerontology (TMIG) and SDS scores after 3months using the FIT home visit program. Further studies with larger sample sizes are needed to elucidate the effect of our FIT home visit program. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
