AB  - The article comments on the study by R. Rosen and colleagues on the effectiveness of vardenafil in improving erectile dysfunction and mild major depressive disorder in men with both disorders. The results of the study describe improved erectile function and decreased depressive symptoms in the active treatment group. The mild severity of depressive symptoms and exclusion of psychiatric comorbidity in the study limits its applicability to those working in secondary care psychiatric services in Great Britain. Suggested interventions include exercise, which can improve both mood and erectile dysfunction.
