AB  - Developed an early identification program for handicapped preschoolers in 2 rural communities. Its goals were to increase parents' ability to detect developmental delays, heighten their awareness of legal rights and human services, and alter their attitudes toward early intervention. Two interventions, mass media and group instruction, were designed and evaluated. 426 parents of preschoolers participated in the interventions. Samples of parents completed needs assessment surveys before and after intervention. Group instruction substantially increased Ss' knowledge of rights and services and motivated them to check their children's development but had no lasting effect on attitudes. Mass media had little effect. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
