AB  - Surveyed 114 administrators of chemical dependency treatment programs (TPs) to determine whether services were provided to youths with chemically impaired parents. Questionnaire responses revealed that therapeutic aids judged most crucial for deterring the negative effects of parental addiction on youths were not usually provided by the TPs. Deterring aids included education on the disease concept of addiction and group, family, and individual counseling. These methods were used with the alcoholic/addict parents but not with their children. Indirect services (e.g., lists of self-help groups) were frequently provided to youths. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
