AB  - Motivational interviewing is a brief treatment approach designed to produce rapid, internally motivated change in addictive behaviors. Motivational interviewing shows promise for engaging clients with dual psychiatric & psychoactive substance use diagnoses in treatment. While initially developed as an individual treatment approach, key motivational enhancement principles may be applied to structured group interventions to facilitate its introduction to inpatient dual-diagnosis treatment. We describe how we developed & pilot-tested a motivational interviewing group for dually diagnosed inpatients, & illustrate successes & pitfalls in clinical implementation. Group participants were readily engaged by the entertaining format & often provocative content, & appeared to benefit from exploration of their ambivalence regarding change. Directions for further development & evaluation are proposed. 9 References. Adapted from the source document.
