AB  - For all therapists who work with Adult Children of Alcoholics this volume provides the first comprehensive and practical guide to group therapy treatment. Combining theory with specific how-to instruction, Dr. Vannicelli introduces the reader to the ACOA literature, explains the rationale for group therapy, describes how to set up a group, and provides a full range of techniques. She offers an unusually insightful examination of countertransference issues, suggests how therapists should prepare for such group work, and proposes areas for future investigation. Exhaustive in its approach, this book will be an ideal resource for any professional treating Adult Children of Alcoholics. The skills and insights offered will also be invaluable for mental health professionals working on family-of-origin issues with other patient populations. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
