AB  - Conducted a retrospective study of 131 patients with severe psychiatric disabilities transferred from a German state hospital to a residential community. A control group consisted of 131 equally disabled patients for whom transfer to the residential community had not materialized. The study centered on the influence of rehabilitation in residential communities on the Ss' work performance. Results show that during a 3-yr period in the residential community the Ss' actual work time increased by 22% to reach 78% of the working time at their disposal. Quality of work improved for Ss in sheltered workshops when they were moved to that more demanding work environment from an occupational therapy installation. (English & Russian abstracts) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
