AB  - Presents the results of an examination of the relationship between weight status and depression levels in a very large sample of inpatients with anorexia nervosa (AN). Depression and anxiety in patients with AN are often attributed to the effects of reduced caloric intake. However, studies that address the link between depression and body weight in anorectic patients are contradictory. Treatment seeking female patients participated in eating disorder-specific group therapy that consisted of nine therapy sessions with 100 min each. Differences in continuous variables between admission and discharge were tested for significance. The findings suggest that depressive symptoms and body mass index (BMI) are not associated in anorectic female patients, neither at admission to an intensive inpatient treatment, nor at discharge. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)
