AB  - Discusses attitudinal data derived from a discussion group of 5 clients in a substance-abuse treatment program who tested positive for human immunodeficiency virus (HIV). Ss' reactions to test results included depression, anxiety, feelings of being experimented on, and a sense of unfinished business with family and friends. There was an increased concern for personal health and for that of significant others. Ss were well aware of possible prejudice, hostility, and rejection. Ss showed increased commitment to treatment and also supported the distribution of clean needles to addicts and community outreach programs that teach abusers to sterilize their equipment to prevent the spread of acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS). (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
