AB  - Proposes that relapse into substance abuse in addicts who have stopped their consumption during a short or long period is also mainly determined by interactions between personal (intrapsychological), family, and social factors, and recollection of the substance's effects. A treatment program in a Dutch therapeutic community and the reentry program linked with it are described. Data from the program show that long-term psychotherapy leads to more favorable results in addicts than few or no therapeutic contacts. Psychotherapeutic issues essential in addictive behavior and in other seriously self-destructive behavior are also discussed, with emphasis on childhood experiences that affect addicts' development. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
