AB  - A psychoanalytic-developmental treatment model is described for use with compulsive freebase cocaine (crack) smokers on an inpatient detoxification unit. Treatment includes individual & group psychotherapy that enables patients to articulate explanations for their drug dependence. Relapse prevention education includes recommendations for aftercare treatment. Psychosocial history & DSM-III diagnostic data for 31 patients reveal histories of dysfunctional family dynamics along with high rates of depressive & personality disorders. A case history illustrates application of the treatment model & problems in currently available postdetoxification treatment. Residential therapeutic communities need to offer variable program lengths & specialized crack residences in therapeutic milieus with trained clinical staff. In addition, they should offer inpatient psychotherapy & family therapy, & provide direct entrance into program-affiliated outpatient services. Recommendations for outpatient services include adjuncts to established anonymous self-help group networks in order to reduce chances of relapse. 3 Tables, 23 References. Modified HA
