AB  - Assesses the perceived service & support delivery needs of persons with developmental disabilities & their families as part of a statewide needs assessment in an upper midwestern state. Six regional focus groups, each comprising 9-11 individuals with disabilities; family members; & professionals from special education, adult services, social services, & rehabilitation, were used to generate ideas. Interactive technology was used in five of the focus groups to minimize the effect of rural & climatic variables. The sixth group was conducted live for purposes of program evaluation. Three major themes resulted from focus group activities & follow-up surveys of 50 participants: (1) preservice staff training, (2) in-service staff training, & (3) program delivery & development. Highlighted are the need for sensitivity, respect, & joint decision making in designing policies for the developmentally disabled. 8 References. Adapted from the source document.
