AB  - Studied the effects of short-term treatment with Gingko biloba extract, EGb 761, on the functional capacities of outpatients with moderate dementia. Human Ss: 40 male and female German middle-aged and old adults (aged 45–70 yrs) (moderate dementia of the Alzheimer and/or vascular type). In a double-blind clinical trial, the Ss were randomly divided into an EGb 761 treatment group and a placebo group. Infusions of EGb 761 or placebo were administered iv 4 days per week for 4 wks. Activities of daily living, cognitive functions, symptoms of depression and general clinical status were evaluated at the beginning and end of treatment. Changes in these parameters were analyzed, and intergroup difference was determined. Tests used: Several German-language instruments, including the Nuremberg Aging Inventory (W. D. Oswald and U. M. Fleischmann, 1995); The Brief Test of General Intelligence (S. Lehri et al, 1980); and a German version of Clinical Global Impressions (NIMH, 1976). (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
