AB  - Inventory, scale, & interview data are used to compare the responses of (M) vs female (F) eating disorder patients (N = 15 & 334, respectively) to intensive day hospital treatment. Ms resemble Fs both at admission & discharge, except in that they show slightly lower scores on the Eating Attitudes Test & Eating Disorders Inventory. M scores remain well above population norms for men. Global clinical outcome is also very similar for both groups. It is concluded that Ms with eating disorders can be treated in intensive group therapy settings where most patients are F, & that their response to treatment is not immediately different to that of F patients. Adapted from the source document.
