AB  - Examined whether family intervention would increase patients' treatment compliance, which is crucial in community care. 77 psychiatric patients (aged 18–80 yrs) with schizophrenia and affective disorder were selected to a controlled trial for 4 mo. The intervention involved drug treatment (with haloperidol) and psychoeducational family intervention. The compliance rate was increased significantly in the trial group compared with the control group (drug treatment only), and Ss in the trial group had better clinical and social outcomes. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2018 APA, all rights reserved)
