AB  - The Double ABCX Model is used as a theoretical framework for discussing the adaptation and adjustment processes of couples who cope with a spouse's mental illness. The mental illness of one spouse is a crisis for the family as a system, as well as for individual family members. It is a chronic stressful event, which couples cope with in accordance with their resources and their perception of stressors. The coping process is a continuous one, and can be characterized along a continuum ranging from maladaptation (destruction of the family, separation, divorce) to bonadaptation (development of resilience, opportunity for growing). Studies highlight the importance of social support as a main resource for the couples' bonadaptation. Therefore, psycho-educational group intervention is designed to provide both spouses with knowledge and social support, and to enhance their skills for communication and problem-solving.
