AB  - After establishing a group therapy program for 17 geriatric outpatients, it was found that: (1) relatively brief socialization opportunities can provide patients with a significant degree of support, (2) small doses of medication can provide rapid and effective control of psychotic symptoms, (3) an intensive case-finding approach is necessary to reach many elderly patients, and (4) nonprofessional workers can provide a great deal of meaningful service. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
