AB  - In an attempt to examine the personality profiles, characteristics, & mental health problems of hysterectomy patients, & offer treatment options (as well as prevention or intervention approaches), a quantitative or qualitative analysis based on a research project & questionnaires given to a sample of women diagnosed with depression or anxiety within 5 years of undergoing hysterectomies (N=19) revealed that the hysterectomy can have a devastating effect on a woman's mental health, resulting in depression, anxiety, loneliness, & low self-esteem. It is concluded that, based on personal clinical experience, group therapy to such patients can be an effective form of treatment for emotional problems. 2 Tables, 6 References. Adapted from the source document.
