AB  - In order to solve the serious impact of excessive use of mobile phones by college students on their learning and physical and mental health, based on the focus of short-term treatment technology, the construction of college students' mobile phone dependence intervention process, that is, clear problems, correct cognition, focus on goals, small walks, mutual supervision, and later Follow 6 links. The empirical research results show that the group counseling model based on the focus on short-term treatment has achieved significant effects in the intervention of withdrawal symptoms, prominent behaviors, social comfort, mood changes, and mobile phone addiction tendencies for college students who rely on mobile phones. To give full play to the role of this model, we should pay attention to the following aspects: the investigation of the mobile phone dependence of college students; practical action plans; the professional quality of group consultants; the coordination and cooperation of schools, society, and families. (English) [ABSTRACT FROM AUTHOR] 为解决大学生过度使用手机对其学习与身心健康产生的严重影响,基于焦点解决短程治疗技术,构建大学生手机依赖干预过程,即明确问题、正确认知、聚焦目标、小步行动、相互监督、后期跟踪6个环节。实证研究结果表明:基于焦点解决短程治疗的团体咨询模式对手机依赖的大学生,在戒断症状、突显行为、社交抚慰、心境改变、手机成瘾倾向方面的干预取得显著效果。要充分发挥该模式的作用,应重视以下几方面的影响:对大学生手机依赖状况的排查工作;切实可行的行动计划;团体咨询者的业务素质;学校、社会、家庭的协同合作. (Chinese) [ABSTRACT FROM AUTHOR] Copyright of Journal of Eastern Liaoning University (Social Sciences) is the property of Department of Journal of Eastern Liaoning University and its content may not be copied or emailed to multiple sites or posted to a listserv without the copyright holder's express written permission. However, users may print, download, or email articles for individual use. This abstract may be abridged. No warranty is given about the accuracy of the copy. Users should refer to the original published version of the material for the full abstract. (Copyright applies to all Abstracts.)
